WEBVTT

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.600
Tsurayuki-kun! Why in the heck did you do it?!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.930
I'm sorry, okay?

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.560
I was hungry, and there was 
nothing else that looked good.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.320
How's that make it okay 
to eat other people's stuff?!

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.740
Seriously, I do feel bad!

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.110
Which is why I went ahead and got 
you some Sukiyamon! See?

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:22.830
<b>Sukiyamon
Soy Flavor</b>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.290
This is is soy sauce-flavored!

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.830
<b>Umakatoyo</b>

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.130
Umakatoyo is tonkotsu-flavored!

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.830
They ain't the same thing!

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.390
I don't get the big deal. 
They're both instant ramen.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.970
<i>Starting this spring, 
along with enrolling in art school,</i>

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.410
They can be the same kinda food, 
but that don't make them the same food!

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:30.960
<i>I've started living in this share house 
with some of my classmates.</i>

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.260
In general terms, they're the same thing!

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.250
Are not!

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.590
<i>It's two guys and two girls, which you think 
would be the ideal roommate setup, and yet...</i>

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.450
They are!

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.560
I want mine back!

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.570
Too bad!

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.600
I heard the whole argument!

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.970
Tsurayuki, seriously, 
eating someone else's food

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.530
is the one of the worst 
things a roommate can do!

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.230
What's wrong? Why'd everyone go so quiet?

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.150
Uh, well, Nanako... Your clothes...

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:56.310
My clothes?

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.890
Quit looking!

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.830
I forgot I was in the middle of changing!

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.880
Hell of a puncher, isn't she?

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.330
<i>For whatever reason, I ended up traveling</i>

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:16.880
<i>ten years into the past 
with my memories intact.</i>

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:24.560
<b>Do not eat other people's food!</b>

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.600
<i>It's what you might call a "time leap."</i>

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.610
<i>My second attempt attempt 
at college has so far been colored</i>

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:24.560
<i>with instant ramen's flavor and
painful hits to the solar plexus,</i>

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.440
<i>along with hope and anxiety.</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.610
<i>It won't be long before 
we start creating for real.</i>

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:35.030
<i>I can't help but wonder what awaits us.</i>

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.460
<b>Comprehensive Exercise</b>

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:16.170
<b>Direction

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:16.170
<b>Performance

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:16.170
When it comes to filmmaking, 
these four areas are going to be crucial.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:21.880
I want you to form groups of four, 
with each person handling one area.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.380
The project is to be three minutes long.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.110
And I mean that seriously,

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:31.140
because once you've all turned 
in your shorts, we'll be screening them.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.970
Everyone's gonna see?

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:35.980
Better make sure it turns out good!

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:40.900
Finally, regarding the theme of the 
short films I want you all to make...

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:46.730
"Time" is kinda broad as far as themes go.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.850
So broad it's hard to know 
where to drill down.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.270
Yeah.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.800
And there's a three-minute 
limit on our runtime, too.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.680
That teacher isn't trying to make this easy!

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.940
It's a good thing we were able to 
pick out our team so quickly, though.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:02.380
Team Kitayama, featuring the roommates 
from Share House Kitayama...

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.440
Kinda on the nose, huh?

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.640
You're directing. Shinoaki's handling
 the technical side.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.270
Nanako's performing, and I'm production...

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:15.610
Well, I wanna do the script, but don't care 
about the performance side of things.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.150
I'm counting on you, Kyoya!

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:22.950
I didn't think we'd end up 
at the same part time job, too.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.250
Tell me about it.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.160
The manager gave me a funny look

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.350
when he noticed we had the same 
address on our applications.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.670
What do you mean?

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:31.880
Forget about it.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.370
Here, hand that over. I'll put it on this shelf.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.320
Say, Nanako...

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.750
Why'd you enroll in art school?

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.980
Is there something you want to do?

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:57.030
There wasn't any real reason.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:00.110
Maybe because I was sick of Lake Biwa?

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.410
The big lake from where you live?

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:03.170
Yeah.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:08.380
When I was in grade school, 
I used to think it was the ocean.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.770
L-Listen, it's seriously huge!

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.750
You would've thought it was 
the ocean at that age, too!

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:22.760
Anyway, there's really nothing else to it...

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.520
I mean, there are towns and stores,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.800
and you can find most things 
you need there.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.530
But I think if I had never left home,

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:31.770
I would've never learned 
what the ocean was really like.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:48.750
The idea of time just passing by 
in a place like that scared me.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:53.040
And before I knew it, here I was.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:58.190
It's embarrassing to admit, but it's 
kind of like I'm here to find myself.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.130
I think I get what you mean.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:20.290
<i>The doors are closing. Please stand clear.</i>

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.790
Are you here for a similar reason?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.130
Yeah.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:46.530
What is it?

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.670
Let me.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.130
This goes up here.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.800
Wait, Nanako...

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.310
Aw, it got caught on something.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.660
Sorry, gimme one second...

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.180
Just one?

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:01.840
Uh, never mind.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.460
Almost done...

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.590
<i>I might be trying to act like I did 
when I was younger,</i>

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:12.460
<i>but I'm still 28 mentally.</i>

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.260
Say, Nanako...

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.610
Uh... thank you.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:18.660
No sweat.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.540
Come on. Let's finish up.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:26.040
<i>I'm sure I don't need to explain how 
I was in no hurry to finish up.</i>

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.000
Get those hands moving, Kyoya.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:40.730
<b>Application

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.730
You're going to fill this in, later, then?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.850
Right. We're still not sure 
what we're doing.

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:48.120
There's no telling when inspiration 
will strike, after all.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.430
Make sure to keep your antennae up.

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.480
Right...

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:55.810
Has anything interesting happened 
lately that you could use?

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:57.370
Lately?

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.920
Well, it sure looks like something has.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.050
You have no idea.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.760
Uh, no, nothing really!

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:12.830
I-If you'll excuse me!

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:19.630
<i>We'd better figure this out soon.</i>

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:22.970
I'm home...

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.190
Shinoaki, you'll catch a cold.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.710
Can't eat another bite...

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.050
Come on. Time to finish eating.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:50.650
Important
 Part

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:49.140
Good morning, Kyoya-kun.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:59.010
That was a real nice dream.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:02.240
I had a bunch of Itoshima oysters to eat.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.480
Sorry to interrupt your meal.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:08.900
Come to think of it, Shinoaki, 
why'd you enroll in art school?

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:14.420
I can't do anything,

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.680
so I wanted to find something I could do.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.440
That's how I ended up here.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.390
That's why you choose art school?

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:22.230
Yeah.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:26.810
I've never been real good at studying, 
even in elementary school.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:29.330
I'd even miss the train a lot.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.560
<i>I can imagine that.</i>

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:36.470
Since it was in the country, missing the
 train meant waiting for a whole half hour.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:39.970
The folks from the station 
even got to know me.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.600
What's wrong?

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:03.560
I think I have an idea 
that goes with our theme!

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:07.340
I'm thinking of having the short 
take place at a train station.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.540
Why a train station?

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.150
Since it's the type of place 
everyone is familiar with,

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:15.080
there's a lot of obvious shorthand 
that'll help people understand the setting.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:19.430
And I think it'd be well-suited to a story 
that wraps up in three minutes.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.350
You've got a point!

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.060
Everybody uses the train.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:36.110
<b>Station</b>

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:27.450
And since stations tend to stay intact 
for long periods of time,

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.610
they work well for depicting 
the passage of time.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.220
My idea is to use that to depict 
the life of one woman

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:36.110
over the course of three minutes.

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:41.530
And I thought it might be good to have her 
life progress in tune with the time of day.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:42.890
What do you think?

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:45.270
Sounds interesting! I think it'll work.

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.100
I like it, too.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.410
I can't wait to see it screened!

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:51.220
What do you think, Tsurayuki?

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:54.800
Can I get a half-hour?

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:58.950
I wonder what that's about.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:10:59.930
I dunno.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.460
What's this?

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:13.440
I wrote up a plot for the 
setup you described.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.400
I figured it was what you were after.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.950
Wow! This is exactly what I meant!

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.300
You're really something, Tsurayuki-kun!

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:23.170
You were able to come up 
with something so quick!

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:25.370
That's better than 
I figured you could manage!

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:30.250
Well, I didn't come up with the idea myself, 
so I figured I should do this much.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.160
That settles it, then!

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.640
No objections!

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.050
Yeah, I'm looking forward to the script—

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.060
Kyoya...

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.230
You got a second?

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.600
What is it, Tsurayuki?

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.390
What's this?

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:55.630
Something from my idea notebook.

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.290
Isn't this—

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.020
It's the exact same thing.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:05.320
Your idea, and what I had 
written down in my notes.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.270
I swear, I didn't see—

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:08.180
Yeah, I know.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.580
I actually had it locked up.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.570
You couldn't possibly have seen it.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:18.780
But you still managed to come up 
with the same idea,

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:20.750
like you read my mind.

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:25.210
It honestly felt like you took 
something right out of my head.

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:27.680
Which is why I rushed 
to write down the outline.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.510
I didn't mean to.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:32.390
It was scary, man, if I'm being honest.

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:39.360
<i>Come to think of it, how exactly 
did I come up with that idea?</i>

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:43.490
<i>I remember now... It was from 
a collection of short stories.</i>

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:48.480
<i>A story about a woman's life, depicted against
 the background of a train station.</i>

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:54.290
<i>I think the impression it left me with 
is what had me imagine something similar.</i>

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:59.670
<i>And I didn't read that book 
until some point in the future.</i>

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:05.420
<i>Does that mean I essentially stole the idea 
from Tsurayuki's future self?</i>

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:11.180
Kyoya, is it just a coincidence?

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:15.590
Or is there something else going on here?

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:23.440
Well, Kyoya? Which one is it?

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.370
Yeah, it couldn't be...

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.460
Sorry about that. 
It has to be a coincidence.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.290
It's not out of the question 
for different people to have the same idea.

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:42.500
You've got a point.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:45.430
I've gotta be honest, I was kind of glad.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:46.710
Why?

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:48.270
A train station makes for an easy setting,

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:51.340
both in terms of the possibility space 
for characters' behavior,

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:53.920
and the things that can happen to them.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:58.900
That's something that you pick up 
from learning about screenwriting.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:04.310
But if anybody here at school 
realized that, I sure didn't notice.

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:06.900
Which is why I was thinking about just 
doing the bare minimum for the project,

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:10.280
and focusing on my individual studies.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:15.580
But I get the feeling we could make 
something good together, Kyoya.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.830
Let's give the teachers 
a real shock with our project!

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:22.610
Yeah!

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.270
<b>The girl_</b>

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.600
What do you mean, you want to make some cuts?!

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:08.050
As things stand, we're going to 
end up going over three  minutes,

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.780
so I was hoping you could 
rewrite the script.

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:13.180
I submitted the script we have 
after already rewriting it a bunch,

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.340
because I thought it was 
the best version of that story!

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:19.480
There's nothing in it 
that can be cut for time!

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.320
Still...

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:26.390
Shinoaki, you can adjust the storyboards 
to make sure everything fits, right?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.450
Let me think...

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.450
It should be doable, but...

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.840
And if we pick up the pace with your lines,

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.960
we can cram them in within 
the time limit, right?

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:37.990
Can we, though?

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:40.260
I mean, I'd have to try...

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:41.920
That's what I'm talking about!

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:44.040
We should at least try first!

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.140
Right?

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:50.750
<i>There's a hard time limit 
on this assignment.</i>

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.590
<i>No matter how good the short turns out,</i>

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:55.550
<i>if we go past that limit, 
we'll be worse off for it.</i>

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.860
<i>But is that good enough a reason 
to convince Tsurayuki?</i>

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.310
<i>Right now, this is probably 
the best I can do.</i>

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:08.030
It's an assignment, after all, so we need 
to follow the rules if we want the credit.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:09.130
So...

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:14.360
Okay. Fine. I'll make the cuts.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.160
Tsurayuki...

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:21.620
Is this your approach when it comes 
to making something good, Kyoya?

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.420
Talk about lame.

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:38.890
Tsurayuki is such a perfectionist!

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:41.980
If it's running long, we should 
just make the cuts!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.670
Don't let it bug you too much.

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:48.690
You there, the young lady stepping on me...

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:54.960
I'm going to refrain from the impulse 
to savor this sensation,

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:56.970
and ask for your help instead.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:17:00.200
If you have any sympathy for your senpai, 
who's run out of money from home,

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.740
and is slowly starving to death...

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.040
<b>Fine Art Study Group</b>

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:06.040
Is this the place?

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.540
Y-Yes, thank you.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:12.170
This is a huge relief.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:15.860
It looks like I was able to make it back, 
thanks to the three of you.

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:19.220
And now, freshmen—

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.340
You're ours!

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:22.890
Nice one, Prez!

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:27.150
Looks like we can avert 
a third year of budget cuts!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.650
We'll be able to survive another year!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.940
I am seriously so sorry!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.630
Sorry about the whole snare.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:36.910
It's not a big deal, so please, stop bowing!

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.960
So, you're going to join the club, right?!

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.830
That is a different matter altogether.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.830
It's no use after all.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:46.140
Please! We're going to be 
in real trouble without new members.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:48.610
Could we at least get permission 
to use your name?

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:49.680
Please, Hashy?!

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:51.840
Please don't come up 
with weird nicknames for me!

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.720
I don't really have time 
for a circle, anyway.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:58.110
I'm thinking about joining.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.330
Yeah, me too, as long as it's 
for a trial period.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:02.220
Seriously?

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.720
Hooray! Hooray!

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:06.580
Hooray!

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:07.590
I...

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:12.690
Fine Art Study Group

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:13.100
I'm Kiryu Takashi, in my fifth year 
of the photography program.

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:15.740
If you have any questions 
about taking pictures, I'm your man.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.110
I'll make time.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.880
<b>Location Release Form</b>

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:38.810
Hashiba Kyoya...

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.970
Oh, chief...

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.290
Er, Kawasegawa-san.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:47.430
Is your team going to be filming 
at the station, too?

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:50.920
Oh... yeah. Yours, too?

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:52.260
You're not going to outdo us.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:55.900
No matter what 
you're putting together,

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:58.700
my team intends to get 
the highest marks.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.360
O...kay.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:03.090
Don't think we're competing 
at the same level.

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:05.090
Because we're not.

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:06.930
We're trying to make something good—

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.080
Then let me ask you...

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:10.710
What's the concept of your short?

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.210
What's the most important element of it?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:15.000
How are you going to use 
the three-minute runtime?

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:17.800
You're handling production, 
so you should have some idea, right?

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:18.970
Well...

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:23.510
Don't underestimate filmmaking.

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.070
Here's the location release form.

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:30.940
Have a seat, and I'll see about 
getting that stamped for you.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.850
Let's see...

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:37.860
Sorry about—

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:41.740
Production's always got something 
to worry about, huh?

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:45.080
I heard your group's got 
some creative differences.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:48.160
Well, uh... Yes.

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:52.490
What's this?

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:55.460
The script of a movie 
that came out the other day.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:58.880
It's had great reception, and seems likely 
to win a few some awards.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.640
But no one seems to like the actual movie.

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:06.630
The director and cast probably 
did whatever they wanted.

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:08.800
The runtime ended up too long, 
ruining the tempo,

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:10.850
and wasting the strengths of the story.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:12.440
This really is hard, isn't it?

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:15.010
A script isn't a finished product.

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:17.450
If the point was to just have 
people read something, and that's all,

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:19.100
it'd be better done as prose.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:22.200
At the script stage, 
it can still go either way.

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:27.760
What you're doing isn't just 
a matter of subtraction.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:31.670
If the production side stops trying, 
then that means the whole project is doomed.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:33.960
That's how important it is.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.670
You're handling production, 
so you should have some idea, right?

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:39.420
Don't underestimate filmmaking.

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.800
I've got one piece of advice for you.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:46.800
Everyone involved in the 
filmmaking process is a creator.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:49.180
And no one outranks anyone else.

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:53.520
Thank you so much!

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:02.160
<i>Whether it's ten years in the past 
or the future, time is limited either way.</i>

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:06.680
<i>Why didn't I realize that sooner?</i>

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:11.140
<i>I have to make sure I have no regrets, 
or nothing will change at all!</i>

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:15.140
Tsurayuki! Tsurayuki!

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:17.130
What? What is it?

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:18.130
I'm sorry, Tsurayuki!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:19.920
What brought this on?!

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:21.450
What? What's up?

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:22.670
What's going on?

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:25.810
I want to talk this over again!

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:27.870
So please, can we make some time for it?

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:32.180
It's already decided. Just do what you want.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:35.810
That's not true! We haven't 
even gotten started yet!

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:37.740
You're right, Tsurayuki!

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:39.860
We haven't filmed anything, 
or started an edit yet,

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:42.060
so it's too soon to give up!

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:43.800
Kyoya...

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:47.580
I want to talk this through as much 
as we can, until the last minute,

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:49.560
so we can decide what we can do 
that'll have the best result!

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:52.400
We'll worry about time later!

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:57.620
If you insist... I'm in, then.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:00.290
Yeah! Let's do this!

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:13.530
Great weather today.

00:22:13.530 --> 00:22:16.110
We picked a day where it was 
supposed to be clear.

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:17.440
There was planning involved.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:21.960
It was hard work getting everything 
to fit into three minutes too, y'know?

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:22.940
Thank you.

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:24.790
Let's make this good.

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:25.660
Yeah!

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:28.950
Oh... This is...

00:22:30.090 --> 00:22:31.270
What is it?

00:22:31.270 --> 00:22:35.780
The camera that Tsurayuki-kun 
borrowed isn't a video camera.

00:22:36.490 --> 00:22:38.130
No, that can't be...

00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:43.460
<b>O Digital Single Lens Reflex Camera
\h\h\h\hDigital Video Camera</b>

00:22:42.150 --> 00:22:43.480
I marked the wrong one.

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:46.260
Why not just go get the right one?

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:48.720
We can't. It'd take too long.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:50.000
Oh, no...

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:52.600
I'm sorry... I can't believe 
it turned out like this...

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:55.870
Hey, everyone makes mistakes. 
Not much we can do.

00:22:55.870 --> 00:22:58.270
Yeah. There's nothing we can do.

00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:02.450
<i>Is there... nothing?</i>

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:14.780
<b>If there's no camera, then we can't film.
If there's no actors, we can't record a performance.
If there's no key art, we don't need to draw anything.
If the writer is missing, we shouldn't bother writing anything.
If there's not enough budget, we'll throw something together.
It is what it is. Nothing we can do about it.
It can't be helped.</b>

00:23:03.510 --> 00:23:06.570
<i>Didn't I spend my life ten years in the future</i>

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:09.550
<i>repeating that excuse, 
and regretting it every time?</i>

00:23:09.550 --> 00:23:12.560
<i>And now, when I've got 
the chance to do it all over...</i>

00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:14.780
<i>Am I going to just do it again?</i>

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:19.740
<i>Make excuses... and kick it all down the road, 
without actually achieving anything?</i>

00:23:19.740 --> 00:23:23.470
<i>Put a hold on everything for ten years, 
and see how that turns out?</i>

00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:27.300
<i>No!</i>

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:28.800
We are not out of options!

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:34.080
We're going to figure something out, damn it!
